@startuml
title RL Maze Explorer - System Context And Data Boundaries
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor User

rectangle "Desktop App" {
  component "Tkinter UI\ncode/ui/app.py\ncode/ui/frames/*\nprofile forms, training controls,\nreports, live visualization" as UI
  component "TrainingController\ncode/services/training.py\nbackground training thread,\nstop checks between episodes,\ncallbacks" as TC
  component "GameEnvironment\ncode/gameEnvironment.py\nshared maze, bot registry,\nprofile application, reset policy" as GE
}

rectangle "Core Services" {
  component "BotFactory\ncode/botFactory.py\nRewardSystem creation,\nconstructor kwarg filtering" as BF
  component "Repository\ncode/services/repository.py\natomic artifact reads/writes" as Repo
  component "Maze + Reward Engine\ncode/maze.py\ncode/rewardSystem.py\nstate, sensors, rewards" as Core
  component "Bot/Profile Config\ncode/bots/__init__.py\ncode/botConfigs.py\nBOT_SPEC discovery,\nconfig rebuilding" as Config
}

rectangle "Bot Implementations" {
  component "BaseBot Contract\ncode/baseBot.py\nreset/calculateState/runEpisode\nlifecycle hooks" as Base
  component "QLearning Bot\ncode/bots/qlearning/*\nQLearningBot + QLearningConfig\nBOT_TYPE/BOT_CLASS/BOT_SPEC" as QL
  component "Future Bots\ncode/bots/<newbot>/*\nsame exports and runtime contract" as FB
}

database "profiles/<profile>/" as Profiles {
  [profile.pkl\nbotType, config,\nrewardConfig, statistics]
  [q_table.pkl\nq_table.checksum]
  [mazes.json\nlatest/highest/lowest\nheatmap snapshots]
  [SimulationRewards.txt\none reward per episode]
  [artifacts/*\nfuture model files]
}

folder "mazes/*.json\nbuilder/fixed-maze files" as Mazes

User --> UI : create/edit profile,\ntrain, visualize, build mazes
UI --> Config : list bot types,\nrender BOT_SPEC params/rewards
UI --> GE : load/apply profiles,\npause visualization,\nset fixed maze
UI --> TC : start(profile, rounds,\nmazeMode, callbacks)
TC --> GE : profileManager.loadProfile(),\napplyProfile(), run bot episode,\nresetEnvironment(), completed count
GE --> BF : createBot(botType,\nconfig, rewards, stats, data)
GE --> Config : discoverBotClasses()\nat startup registration
BF --> QL : instantiate registered type
BF --> FB : instantiate future registered type
BF --> Core : create RewardSystem\nwith MazeSensors
QL -up-|> Base
FB -up-|> Base
QL --> Repo : Q-table and training artifacts
FB --> Repo : optional modelArtifactsDir()\nor custom artifacts
GE --> Repo : shared repository,\nensureMazeFile()
Repo --> Profiles : persistent profile state
GE --> Core : maze reset/state,\nreward dependencies
UI --> Mazes : load/save fixed custom mazes
Core --> Mazes : setState()/getState() data shape

note bottom of UI
  BOT_SPEC currently renders profile controls, but saveProfile()
  only constructs QLearningConfig unless custom save logic is added.
  Specialized controls also belong in CreateEditProfileFrame and/or
  VisualizationFrame.
end note

note bottom of Repo
  Training writes are centralized here.
  Visualization should stay inference-only and avoid durable writes.
end note

@enduml
